{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101774","id":2285841199,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6IPysv","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101774","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101774.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101774.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101774","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101774/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101774/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101774/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/84d3adcf2f6544d30a5f832311ccc79b9412f11f","number":101774,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Wayland: Implement native sub-windows","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"*psss... the text of this PR got completely rewritten now that it's ready. If you want to see the original version, use GH's history feature* \r\n\r\nEverything below will be extremely boring. So, here's a pretty picture of the editor running on sway:\r\n\r\n![Godot running on sway with multiple native windows](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6e16df47-52b7-45a2-8fb2-2f1d60220dc0)\r\n\r\nI mean, it's still probably somewhat boring but that's the nature of what I do :P\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe backend is now mature enough to not explode with multiple windows but the `DisplayServer` API still cannot meet some guarantees required by the various Wayland protocols we use. To meet those guarantees this patch adds three new elements to the DisplayServer API, with relative handling logic for `Window` and `Popup` nodes:\r\n\r\n - `WINDOW_EVENT_FORCE_CLOSE`, which tells a window to *forcefully* close itself and ensure a proper cleanup of its references, as Wayland enforces this behavior;\r\n - `WINDOW_FLAG_POPUP_WM_HINT`, which explicitly declares a window as a \"popup\", as Wayland enforces this distinction and heuristics are not reliable enough;\r\n - `FEATURE_SELF_FITTING_WINDOWS`, which signals that the compositor can fit windows to the screen automatically and that nodes should not do that themselves.\r\n\r\nGiven the size of this feature, this patch also includes various `WaylandThread` reworks and fixes including:\r\n\r\n - Improvements to frame wait logic, ~with fixes to various stalls~ and a configurable (through a `#define`) timeout amount; **Edit**: stalls fixed in #102674. \r\n - A proper implementation of `window_can_draw`;\r\n - Complete overhaul of pointer and tablet handling. Now everything is always accumulated and handled only on each respective `frame` event. This makes their logic simpler and more robust.\r\n - Better handling of pointer leaving and pointer enter/exit event sending;\r\n - Keyboard focus tracking;\r\n - More solid window references using IDs instead of raw pointers as windows can be deleted at any time;\r\n - More aggressive messaging to window nodes to enforce rects imposed by the compositor.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nThe new APIs that I added will be useful for other `DisplayServer` implementations too, perhaps with the exception of `FEATURE_SELF_FITTING_WINDOWS`.\r\n\r\nAs you can see, this PR includes also _a lot_ of core improvements and fixes to stuff that became more evident while testing multiple windows. I'm definitely going to backport/separate some of those.\r\n\r\nIt does not even include the FIFO additions (#101454) or fixes for some leftover issues that @arlo-phoenix [found in the original PR](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/57025#issuecomment-1839003787) (mainly I think only missing keyboard composition) so once everything is done the Wayland experience should become even more solid.\r\n\r\n## Known issues\r\n\r\n- There's some error spam while starting the editor. It's an engine bug triggered by the fact that now we have a proper implementation of `window_can_draw`: #100900\r\n\r\n- I forgot to account for `wl_pointer::frame` missing on very old compositors.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097326,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTczMjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/platform:linuxbsd","name":"platform:linuxbsd","description":"","color":"e4e4e4","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098255,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyNTU=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:platforms","name":"topic:platforms","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone